00:21:54.401 --> 00:22:45.891
You know when you Yeah, and it comes in so hot just like shot through the heart like it comes It's another song it comes in like that's what got whittled down to this like death match between those two songs And we were almost shouting at each other about like and I I was I was of the moment Bon Jovi, you know I was like a teenager preteen at that moment that song just hit at that point for me much more than journey was you know 10 15 years before that and so I think I think I might have made the final call like it's gotta be it's got to be I remember I do remember in the network run through I think Dave Bakers was was just pressing play every time Yeah, you know off and I do remember it killing It's funny every time and it gets funnier and it's also like when Kobe starts singing it when Robin Yeah, singing it up the car is so funny.
你知道当，是的，它一出来就那么火热，就像直击心脏一样，它出来……是另一首歌，它出来的方式就像……最后这两首歌被精简下来，成了它们之间的生死决斗，我们当时几乎都要冲对方大喊大叫了，关于……而且我，我当时更倾向于邦·乔维（Bon Jovi），你知道的，我当时是个十几岁的少年/前青少年，那首歌在那时对我的触动远大于十到十五年前的 Journey，所以我想，我可能拍板做了最终决定，就得是这首，就是它。我记得，我确实记得在电视台的彩排中，戴夫·贝克斯（Dave Bakers）好像每次都直接按播放键，对，你知道的，关掉，而且我确实记得它效果炸裂。每次都很好笑，而且越来越好笑，还有就是科比（Kobe）开始唱的时候，罗宾——对，跟着唱的时候，在车里那段太搞笑了。

